/* F's first parameter is named br, and F returns bad on the input b, which
   qo rejects: the property is violated.  The reduction joins the branches
   of F's case with its choice terminal br, and a scheme in which that
   terminal sits under a parameter of the same name reads the parameter
   instead, choosing one branch where both must be accepted. */
%BEGING
F br xs -> case xs of
  a => ok
| b => bad.
%ENDG

%BEGINA
qs a -> .
qs b -> .
qo ok -> .
%ENDA

%BEGINT
F : qs -> qs -> qo.
%ENDT
